### Patent-Style Description

A labeling apparatus **(100)** is provided for applying labels **(102)** to products **(104)** conveyed along a transport path in a transport direction **(T)**. The labeling apparatus **(100)** comprises a label supply assembly **(110)** configured to advance a backing strip **(112)** carrying a plurality of removably adhered labels **(102)**. A dispensing member **(114)** separates each label **(102)** from the backing strip **(112)** and dispenses the separated label generally along an imaginary dispensing line **(D)** toward a movable applicator **(120)**.

The movable applicator **(120)** includes a label-receiving surface **(122)** and is movable between a label-receiving position **(124)** and a label-application position **(126)**. An alignment roller **(130)** is positioned such that at least a portion of the alignment roller **(130)** intersects the imaginary dispensing line **(D)**. The alignment roller **(130)** is configured to engage the dispensed label **(102)** and control at least one of the lateral position, angular orientation, or longitudinal position of the label **(102)** relative to the label-receiving surface **(122)**.

A transport system **(140)** conveys the products **(104)** in the transport direction **(T)** through an application region **(142)**. A controller **(150)** coordinates operation of the label supply assembly **(110)**, the movable applicator **(120)**, the alignment roller **(130)**, and the transport system **(140)** such that each aligned label **(102)** is transferred from the movable applicator **(120)** to a predetermined location on a respective product **(104)**.

### Exemplary Independent Apparatus Claim

1. A labeling apparatus **(100)** comprising:  
   a label supply assembly **(110)** configured to advance a backing strip **(112)** carrying a plurality of labels **(102)**;  
   a dispensing member **(114)** configured to remove a label **(102)** from the backing strip **(112)** and dispense the label **(102)** generally along an imaginary dispensing line **(D)**;  
   a movable applicator **(120)** positioned to receive the dispensed label **(102)** and configured to transfer the label **(102)** to a product **(104)**;  
   an alignment roller **(130)** positioned so as to intersect the imaginary dispensing line **(D)** and configured to engage and align the label **(102)** relative to the movable applicator **(120)**; and  
   a transport system **(140)** configured to move the product **(104)** in a transport direction **(T)** through an application region **(142)** in which the movable applicator **(120)** applies the aligned label **(102)** to the product **(104)**.

### Exemplary Independent Method Claim

2. A method of applying a label **(102)** to a product **(104)**, the method comprising:  
   advancing a backing strip **(112)** carrying the label **(102)**;  
   separating the label **(102)** from the backing strip **(112)** using a dispensing member **(114)**;  
   dispensing the separated label **(102)** generally along an imaginary dispensing line **(D)** toward a movable applicator **(120)**;  
   engaging the label **(102)** with an alignment roller **(130)** intersecting the imaginary dispensing line **(D)**, thereby aligning the label **(102)** on the movable applicator **(120)**;  
   conveying the product **(104)** in a transport direction **(T)**; and  
   moving the movable applicator **(120)** to apply the aligned label **(102)** at a predetermined location on the product **(104)**.
